WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:11.115
Marvin was a goldfish who lived in a pond in Lily's backyard.

2
00:00:11.116 --> 00:00:15.809
Every day, Lily would feed all the goldfish.

3
00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:21.186
She loved to watch them swim about and gave each one a name.

4
00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:30.795
Marvin was her favorite because he had an especially long and beautiful tail.

5
00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:32.998
Marvin loved his home.

6
00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:40.161
He loved to swim in the clear, green water and play among the lily pads and tall reeds.

7
00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:43.503
Best of all, there was a waterfall.

8
00:00:43.504 --> 00:00:46.855
The pond was just perfect.

9
00:00:46.856 --> 00:00:52.457
Marvin couldn't imagine living anywhere else.

10
00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:58.512
One day, Marvin heard a frog bragging about what he did outside the pond.

11
00:00:58.513 --> 00:01:03.614
"There's way more to do out there," said the frog.

12
00:01:03.615 --> 00:01:12.699
"More bugs to catch, and there are rabbits and squirrels─all kinds of new things to see."

13
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.934
Suddenly, the pond didn't seem so great anymore.

14
00:01:16.935 --> 00:01:19.327
But Marvin was a fish.

15
00:01:19.328 --> 00:01:23.579
He couldn't go anywhere without water.

16
00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:28.759
"Wait," he thought, "where is there more water than in this pond?

17
00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:33.957
The sea! It's bigger than big!"

18
00:01:33.958 --> 00:01:40.761
He thought of the fantastic sea creatures he'd meet, and the secret caves he'd discover.

19
00:01:40.762 --> 00:01:42.697
He had to get there.

20
00:01:42.698 --> 00:01:45.327
Marvin soon became grumpy.

21
00:01:45.328 --> 00:01:47.569
His friends noticed.

22
00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:53.375
"Why are you sad?" they asked.

23
00:01:53.376 --> 00:01:55.371
"I don't like it here anymore.

24
00:01:55.372 --> 00:01:58.685
I want to be out in the deep blue sea!"

25
00:01:58.686 --> 00:02:04.319
"Yeah, in your dreams!" they laughed.

26
00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.129
But Marvin wouldn't give up his dream.

27
00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.982
One night, there was a rainstorm.

28
00:02:10.983 --> 00:02:15.993
The water in the pond started to rise.

29
00:02:15.994 --> 00:02:20.814
"This could be my only chance to get out of here!" thought Marvin.

30
00:02:20.815 --> 00:02:27.974
When the water seemed high enough, he swam right over the rocks around the pond.

31
00:02:27.975 --> 00:02:29.807
He was free!

32
00:02:29.808 --> 00:02:38.646
The rainwater carried him to a stream, where he swam and swam.

33
00:02:38.647 --> 00:02:42.986
Suddenly, a huge turtle dived in beside him.

34
00:02:42.987 --> 00:02:49.476
It made such a big splash that Marvin sailed up in the air.

35
00:02:49.477 --> 00:02:54.561
He landed in a puddle surrounded by tall weeds.

36
00:02:54.562 --> 00:02:56.498
He was stuck!

37
00:02:56.499 --> 00:03:00.398
Marvin was scared and all alone.

38
00:03:00.399 --> 00:03:05.123
What was he going to do?

39
00:03:05.124 --> 00:03:10.125
The next morning, Lily ran to the pond and found Marvin missing.

40
00:03:10.126 --> 00:03:12.322
Her heart was broken.

41
00:03:12.323 --> 00:03:16.262
Her parents tried to make her feel better.

42
00:03:16.263 --> 00:03:23.840
"We'll get a new fish," they said, "one like Marvin."

43
00:03:23.841 --> 00:03:26.148
Lily shook her head.

44
00:03:26.149 --> 00:03:28.297
"No one could be like Marvin.

45
00:03:28.298 --> 00:03:31.542
He was the best fish in the world."

46
00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:38.863
Meanwhile, a boy was walking by the stream and saw Marvin trying to get out of the puddle.

47
00:03:38.864 --> 00:03:44.744
He carefully scooped him up in a cup.

48
00:03:44.745 --> 00:03:53.057
For what seemed like a very long time, Marvin was cramped in a small, dark container.

49
00:03:53.058 --> 00:03:59.554
Then he was dumped into a crowded glass tank with strange fish.

50
00:03:59.555 --> 00:04:05.787
Weird people would stare at him and tap on the glass.

51
00:04:05.788 --> 00:04:11.735
"Oh, how I wish I were back in the pond again with my friends," sighed Marvin.

52
00:04:11.736 --> 00:04:13.839
"This is terrible."

53
00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:22.577
Days went by, and Marvin began to lose hope of ever going home again.

54
00:04:22.578 --> 00:04:26.216
He began to sink lower and lower in the tank.

55
00:04:26.217 --> 00:04:30.296
Pretty soon he just stayed on the bottom.

56
00:04:30.297 --> 00:04:35.185
Then, to his amazement, he saw Lily!

57
00:04:35.186 --> 00:04:41.127
Her parents had taken her to the pet store where Marvin had ended up.

58
00:04:41.128 --> 00:04:47.657
She was looking at the fish in each of the tanks.

59
00:04:47.658 --> 00:04:59.847
Marvin swam right up to the glass and wiggled his long tail back and forth as fast as he could, trying to get her attention.

60
00:04:59.848 --> 00:05:01.325
"Mom and Dad, look!

61
00:05:01.326 --> 00:05:04.924
I found Marvin!" Lily cried.

62
00:05:04.925 --> 00:05:11.414
She brought him home right away.

63
00:05:11.415 --> 00:05:15.920
Marvin was very happy to be back in the pond.

64
00:05:15.921 --> 00:05:20.459
"Did you get to the sea?" his friends asked.

65
00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:25.738
"It wasn't exactly what I thought it would be," he said with a sly grin.

66
00:05:25.739 --> 00:05:32.441
"Home is much better."
